@segment 47-50 Stranglethorn III & Booty Bay
@start-level 47
# Human Mage (from the Skyborne Mage route) segment. Same quests, order, bind (Booty Bay) and flights as the source-route segment this
# was copied from. Deviations:
# - All combat hints rewritten for a mage (Frostbolt from range, Frost Nova and step back, Polymorph on a second
#   humanoid or beast, Counterspell as the interrupt).
# - "H Booty Bay" after the north loop is the plain Hearthstone, its first use in the segment (unchanged).
# - The optional training trip at the very end is now Teleport: Stormwind (one Rune of Teleportation) -> Jennea Cannon
#   (level 48 and 50 spells) -> Hearthstone back to Booty Bay, where the boat leaves. The Hearthstone was last used
#   before the Wild Shore, the three ships and the level 50 grind, far more than an hour earlier, and it is not needed
#   again until Azshara (segment 22).
# - Added on that trip: the level 50 mage quest 8250 Magecraft (Elsharin, beside the mage trainers). The grind to 50
#   comes just before, so the character is 50 there. It is carried through Un'Goro (segment 21) to Sanath Lim-yo in
#   Azshara (segment 22). This is the only Stormwind stop at 50+ before Azshara.
# Carried in (segment 19's carry-out): 2767, 648 and 836 (the three robot escorts), 669 Sunken Treasure and
# 209 Skullsplitter Tusks (tusks still to collect), all for Booty Bay; 4450 Ledger from Tanaris (Gadgetzan, segment 21).
@carry 209,648,669,836,2767,4450
# Done in segment 15: 599 unlocks The Bloodsail Buccaneers (604), 607 unlocks Voodoo Dues, 595 unlocks Up to Snuff and
# Keep An Eye Out. The rest are the prerequisites of the carried quests: 189 -> 209, 668 -> 669, 351 -> 648, 485 -> 836,
# 2766 -> 2767, 4449 -> 4450.
@done 599,607,595,189,668,351,485,2766,4449
# Order: Nethergarde -> Booty Bay (hearth) -> north loop (naga, gorillas, Unbagwa, Zanzil's ruins, Skullsplitter tusks) ->
# Booty Bay -> Wild Shore -> Booty Bay -> bottle, Jaguero Isle, the three ships and the level 50 grind -> Booty Bay -> (Stormwind to train and take Magecraft, hearth back) -> Ratchet boat.
# Carried out (2): 4450 Ledger from Tanaris, 8250 Magecraft (if taken).

# ---------- Booty Bay ----------
FLY Booty Bay | Alexandra Constantine, the Nethergarde Keep gryphon master. The flight goes by Darkshire.
S Booty Bay | Innkeeper Skindle (27.0, 77.3)
T 2767,648,836 | Oglethorpe Obnoticus, the gnome engineer (28.4, 76.3). Hand in each robot you rescued.
A 3721 | Oglethorpe Obnoticus offers An OOX of Your Own only if you rescued all three robots. Missed one? Skip this step and the next.
T 3721 | Oglethorpe Obnoticus
T 669 | Fleet Master Seahorn (27.2, 77.0). Leave the second Sunken Treasure.
A 604 | Fleet Master Seahorn
A 609 | "Sea Wolf" MacKinley (27.8, 77.1)
A 621 | Crank Fizzlebub, next to the innkeeper (27.1, 77.2)
A 617 | Privateer Bloads (26.8, 76.4)
A 587 | Deeg (26.9, 77.3)
A 576 | Dizzy One-Eye (28.6, 75.9)
A 348 | Fin Fizracket, lying sick (27.6, 76.7)

# ---------- North loop ----------
C 617 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 26.2, 62.0 | Leave Booty Bay through the tunnel and ride north-west to the coast. Naga Explorers (43-44) on the beach and in the shallows (24-28, 59-65) drop the 10 Bundles of Akiris Reed, about 1 in 3.
N Get a Gorilla Fang from the Elder Mistvale Gorillas @ Stranglethorn Vale, 32.9, 64.6 | Mistvale Valley, just east of the naga beach. Elder Mistvale Gorillas (40-41) and Silverback Patriarchs (42-43) drop it. You need one for the witch doctor.
C 348 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 35.3, 60.4 | Witch Doctor Unbagwa stands in a small cave at the north end of the valley (35.3, 60.4). Give him the Gorilla Fang: he summons three gorillas, one after another. The last, Mokk the Savage (44), drops the Heart of Mokk. Eat and drink to full before you talk to him. Three fights in a row: stand back from him, Frost Nova each gorilla when it reaches you, step back and Frostbolt it down. Mana Shield if Mokk gets on you with your mana still high; bandage between gorillas.
C 609:3 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 40.0, 58.2 | Ride east to the Ruins of Aboraz. Chucky "Ten Thumbs" (43-44) stands in the ruins and drops Chucky's Huge Ring.
C 621 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 38.2, 56.0 | Zanzil's Zombies, Hunters, Witch Doctors and Naga (43-44) in and around the Ruins of Aboraz drop the 12 Zanzil's Mixture, about 1 in 3. They stand close together: pull one with Frostbolt from range, Polymorph a second one (not the Zombies: they are undead), and Counterspell the Witch Doctors' casts.
C 609:1 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 35.3, 51.3 | Ride north-west to the Ruins of Jubuwal. Maury "Club Foot" Wilkins drops Maury's Clubbed Foot.
C 609:2 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 34.9, 51.8 | Jon-Jon the Crow stands next to him and drops Jon-Jon's Golden Spyglass. Fight the two one at a time; the zombies around them also drop mixture.
C 209 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 45.6, 40.0 | Ride north-east to the Skullsplitter troll ruins east of the road (42-48, 33-44). Every Skullsplitter troll drops tusks, about 1 in 5: you need 18. They are level 39-44 and pay little experience now: if you would rather not ride there, abandon Skullsplitter Tusks and skip its hand-in.
H Booty Bay | Hearthstone: its first use in this segment. It saves the ride back down the whole zone.
T 209 | Kebok (27.0, 77.1)
T 617 | Privateer Bloads. Leave the second Akiris by the Bundle.
T 609 | "Sea Wolf" MacKinley. His next quest, Cracking Maury's Foot, is elite: leave it.
T 621 | Crank Fizzlebub
T 348 | Fin Fizracket

# ---------- Wild Shore ----------
C 604 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 27.3, 82.8 | The Bloodsail camp on the Wild Shore, the beach south of Booty Bay. Kill 10 Bloodsail Swashbucklers (41-43); the Bloodsail Charts and the Bloodsail Orders are papers lying in the camp (27.2, 82.7 and 27.7, 83.1). Every pirate can drop Snuff for Deeg and Dizzy's Eye: loot them all. Counterspell a Warlock's cast, or Polymorph him and kill him last.
T 604 | Back in Booty Bay: Fleet Master Seahorn
A 608 | Fleet Master Seahorn

# ---------- The bottle, the ships and the level 50 grind ----------
A 594 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 32.8, 78.7 | Leave through the tunnel and go down to the beach east of Booty Bay. Open a Half-Buried Bottle on the sand (they lie all along this coast) and right-click the Carefully Folded Note inside.
T 594 | Swim south-east to Jaguero Isle: Princess Poobah (38.5, 80.6). Skymane Gorillas (50) roam the isle and King Mukla (51 elite) is at its south end: go straight to her. Her next quest is elite: leave it.
C 608 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 30.9, 89.0 | Swim west to the three Bloodsail ships anchored off the Wild Shore. Captain Stillwater (45-46) is on the eastern ship (32.9, 88.2), Captain Keelhaul (46-47) on the western one (29.3, 88.3), Fleet Master Firallon (48) on the southern one (30.6, 90.6). In Classic each captain stands in his ship's cabin with one or two guards: clear the deck first, pull the guards out one at a time; when two come, Polymorph one, Frost Nova the other, step back and kill them one by one.
C 587,576 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 30.9, 89.0 | The ship crews drop the rest of the 15 Snuff and Dizzy's Eye.
L 50 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 30.9, 89.0 | The second big grind of the route. Stay on the three ships (Bloodsail Sea Dogs, Elder Magi and deckhands, 43-48; they respawn fast) until level 50. Counterspell the Elder Magi; conjure water before you start and drink between pulls. For a change of scene: Zanzil's undead at the Ruins of Aboraz (38, 56). Mobs here are turning green, so it is slow: you can also stop early and finish this level on the Dunemaul ogres in Tanaris (46-48) or in Un'Goro Crater at the start of the next segment, where Bungle in the Jungle needs level 50. But your level 50 class quest is handed out in Stormwind in a moment and nowhere else on the way: reaching 50 here is worth it.
T 608 | Back in Booty Bay: Fleet Master Seahorn
T 587 | Deeg
T 576 | Dizzy One-Eye
N No Mithril Casing yet? Look for one before you sail | You need it for A-Me 01 in Un'Goro Crater. Booty Bay and Gadgetzan had auction houses in Classic; an engineer can make one.
N Cast Teleport: Stormwind | A training trip before you leave the continent: there is no mage trainer on the way through Tanaris, Un'Goro and Azshara. It costs one Rune of Teleportation. Your Hearthstone must be ready for the way back (you last used it before the Wild Shore). Still on cooldown, or short of level 48? Skip this step and the next three.
TRAIN @ Stormwind City, 49.6, 85.8 | Stormwind, Wizard's Sanctum in the Mage Quarter: Jennea Cannon (49.6, 85.8). Learn your level 48 and 50 spells. Buy 5 Runes of Teleportation from a reagent vendor: the next mage trainer visit is another teleport, from Azshara.
A 8250 @ Stormwind City, 48.2, 87.2 | Magecraft from Elsharin, beside the mage trainers (48.2, 87.2). Needs level 50. It ends at Sanath Lim-yo in Azshara, two segments on: keep it in the log through Un'Goro. Still 49? She will not offer it: skip this step (the next Stormwind stop comes only after Azshara, see segment 22).
H Booty Bay | Hearthstone back to the inn; the dock is just below.
N Take the boat from the Booty Bay dock to Ratchet | Your hearthstone stays set to Booty Bay until Gadgetzan. Keep 4450 Ledger from Tanaris and 8250 Magecraft.
